# C++ Conventions

- Follow `.clang-format`: LLVM base style, 2-space indentation, attached braces, 100-column limit, sorted includes, and left-aligned pointers/references.
- Use the existing `noria` namespace and PascalCase types; use camelCase functions and variables.
- Compile as standard C++20 with no compiler extensions. Keep `-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic` clean.
- Prefer value semantics and RAII. Use `std::unique_ptr` for AST ownership and references for required non-owning access.
- Mark single-argument constructors `explicit`; mark closed derived AST node types `final`; use `override` when overriding virtual functions.
- Prefer `std::string_view` for read-only non-owning text when lifetime is clear, but store owned token text, names, and diagnostics as `std::string`.
- Use `const` and `auto` where they improve clarity; do not hide important numeric or LLVM types.
- Use scoped enums and named constants instead of magic values.
- Keep helpers file-local in an anonymous namespace unless they are part of a public compiler-stage interface.
- Favor direct, readable control flow over forced STL algorithms or premature abstraction.

# Change Discipline

- Format changed C++ files before handoff; `just format` formats `include/noria/*.hpp` and `src/*.cpp`.
- Do not perform unrelated repository-wide reformatting.
- Add a new source file to the relevant CMake target in the same change.
- Keep public declarations in `include/noria/` and implementations in `src/`.
